{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.121.3",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-48384-git",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-48384 high vulnerability for git package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Git is a fast, scalable, distributed revision control system with an unusually rich command set that provides both high-level operations and full access to internals. When reading a config value, Git strips any trailing carriage return and line feed (CRLF). When writing a config entry, values with a trailing CR are not quoted, causing the CR to be lost when the config is later read. When initializing a submodule, if the submodule path contains a trailing CR, the altered path is read resulting in the submodule being checked out to an incorrect location. If a symlink exists that points the altered path to the submodule hooks directory, and the submodule contains an executable post-checkout hook, the script may be unintentionally executed after checkout. This vulnerability is fixed in v2.43.7, v2.44.4, v2.45.4, v2.46.4, v2.47.3, v2.48.2, v2.49.1, and v2.50.1."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-48384",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-48384\nSeverity: high\nPackage: git\nVersion: 1:2.30.2-1\nFix Version: 1:2.30.2-1+deb11u5\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2025-48384](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-48384)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-48384**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | git  | 1:2.30.2-1  | 1:2.30.2-1+deb11u5  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2025-48384](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-48384)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/git@1%3A2.30.2-1?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-48384-git-man",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-48384 high vulnerability for git-man package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Git is a fast, scalable, distributed revision control system with an unusually rich command set that provides both high-level operations and full access to internals. When reading a config value, Git strips any trailing carriage return and line feed (CRLF). When writing a config entry, values with a trailing CR are not quoted, causing the CR to be lost when the config is later read. When initializing a submodule, if the submodule path contains a trailing CR, the altered path is read resulting in the submodule being checked out to an incorrect location. If a symlink exists that points the altered path to the submodule hooks directory, and the submodule contains an executable post-checkout hook, the script may be unintentionally executed after checkout. This vulnerability is fixed in v2.43.7, v2.44.4, v2.45.4, v2.46.4, v2.47.3, v2.48.2, v2.49.1, and v2.50.1."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-48384",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-48384\nSeverity: high\nPackage: git-man\nVersion: 1:2.30.2-1\nFix Version: 1:2.30.2-1+deb11u5\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2025-48384](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-48384)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-48384**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | git-man  | 1:2.30.2-1  | 1:2.30.2-1+deb11u5  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2025-48384](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-48384)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/git-man@1%3A2.30.2-1?arch=all\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=git"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-4911-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-4911 high vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A buffer overflow was discovered in the GNU C Library's dynamic loader ld.so while processing the GLIBC_TUNABLES environment variable. This issue could allow a local attacker to use maliciously crafted GLIBC_TUNABLES environment variables when launching binaries with SUID permission to execute code with elevated privileges."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-4911",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-4911\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.31-13+deb11u5\nFix Version: 2.31-13+deb11u7\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2023-4911](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-4911)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-4911**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libc-bin  | 2.31-13+deb11u5  | 2.31-13+deb11u7  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2023-4911](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-4911)  |\n"
