            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-38545-libcurl4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-38545 critical vulnerability for libcurl4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "This flaw makes curl overflow a heap based buffer in the SOCKS5 proxy handshake.  When curl is asked to pass along the host name to the SOCKS5 proxy to allow that to resolve the address instead of it getting done by curl itself, the maximum length that host name can be is 255 bytes.  If the host name is detected to be longer, curl switches to local name resolving and instead passes on the resolved address only. Due to this bug, the local variable that means \"let the host resolve the name\" could get the wrong value during a slow SOCKS5 handshake, and contrary to the intention, copy the too long host name to the target buffer instead of copying just the resolved address there.  The target buffer being a heap based buffer, and the host name coming from the URL that curl has been told to operate with."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-38545",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-38545\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: libcurl4\nVersion: 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u3\nFix Version: 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u10\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2023-38545](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-38545)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-38545**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | libcurl4  | 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u3  | 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u10  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2023-38545](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-38545)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u3?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45288-go",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45288 high vulnerability for go package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An attacker may cause an HTTP/2 endpoint to read arbitrary amounts of header data by sending an excessive number of CONTINUATION frames. Maintaining HPACK state requires parsing and processing all HEADERS and CONTINUATION frames on a connection. When a request's headers exceed MaxHeaderBytes, no memory is allocated to store the excess headers, but they are still parsed. This permits an attacker to cause an HTTP/2 endpoint to read arbitrary amounts of header data, all associated with a request which is going to be rejected. These headers can include Huffman-encoded data which is significantly more expensive for the receiver to decode than for an attacker to send. The fix sets a limit on the amount of excess header frames we will process before closing a connection."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45288",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-45288\nSeverity: high\nPackage: go\nVersion: 1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.21.9,1.22.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/go/bin/go\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-45288](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45288)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-45288**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | go  | 1.18.10  | 1.21.9,1.22.2  | binary  | /usr/local/go/bin/go  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-45288](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45288)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/go@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
