            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-51385-openssh-client",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-51385 medium vulnerability for openssh-client package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In ssh in OpenSSH before 9.6, OS command injection might occur if a user name or host name has shell metacharacters, and this name is referenced by an expansion token in certain situations. For example, an untrusted Git repository can have a submodule with shell metacharacters in a user name or host name."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-51385",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-51385\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: openssh-client\nVersion: 1:8.4p1-5+deb11u1\nFix Version: 1:8.4p1-5+deb11u3\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2023-51385](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-51385)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-51385**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | openssh-client  | 1:8.4p1-5+deb11u1  | 1:8.4p1-5+deb11u3  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2023-51385](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-51385)  |\n"
              },
