            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45283-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45283 high vulnerability for stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The filepath package does not recognize paths with a \\??\\ prefix as special.\n\nOn Windows, a path beginning with \\??\\ is a Root Local Device path equivalent to a path beginning with \\\\?\\. Paths with a \\??\\ prefix may be used to access arbitrary locations on the system. For example, the path \\??\\c:\\x is equivalent to the more common path c:\\x.\n\nBefore fix, Clean could convert a rooted path such as \\a\\..\\??\\b into the root local device path \\??\\b. Clean will now convert this to .\\??\\b.\n\nSimilarly, Join(\\, ??, b) could convert a seemingly innocent sequence of path elements into the root local device path \\??\\b. Join will now convert this to \\.\\??\\b.\n\nIn addition, with fix, IsAbs now correctly reports paths beginning with \\??\\ as absolute, and VolumeName correctly reports the \\??\\ prefix as a volume name.\n\nUPDATE: Go 1.20.11 and Go 1.21.4 inadvertently changed the definition of the volume name in Windows paths starting with \\?, resulting in filepath.Clean(\\?\\c:) returning \\?\\c: rather than \\?\\c:\\ (among other effects). The previous behavior has been restored."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://go.dev/issue/63713",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-45283\nSeverity: high\nPackage: stdlib\nVersion: go1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.20.11,1.21.4\nType: go-module\nLocation: /usr/local/go/bin/go\nData Namespace: govulndb:language:go\nLink: [CVE-2023-45283](https://go.dev/issue/63713)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-45283**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | stdlib  | go1.18.10  | 1.20.11,1.21.4  | go-module  | /usr/local/go/bin/go  | govulndb:language:go  | [CVE-2023-45283](https://go.dev/issue/63713)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:golang/stdlib@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-45061-libpython3.9-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-45061 high vulnerability for libpython3.9-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An issue was discovered in Python before 3.11.1. An unnecessary quadratic algorithm exists in one path when processing some inputs to the IDNA (RFC 3490) decoder, such that a crafted, unreasonably long name being presented to the decoder could lead to a CPU denial of service. Hostnames are often supplied by remote servers that could be controlled by a malicious actor; in such a scenario, they could trigger excessive CPU consumption on the client attempting to make use of an attacker-supplied supposed hostname. For example, the attack payload could be placed in the Location header of an HTTP response with status code 302. A fix is planned in 3.11.1, 3.10.9, 3.9.16, 3.8.16, and 3.7.16."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2022-45061",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-45061\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libpython3.9-minimal\nVersion: 3.9.2-1\nFix Version: 3.9.2-1+deb11u2\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2022-45061](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2022-45061)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2022-45061**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libpython3.9-minimal  | 3.9.2-1  | 3.9.2-1+deb11u2  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2022-45061](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2022-45061)  |\n"
