            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-43552-libcurl4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-43552 medium vulnerability for libcurl4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A use after free vulnerability exists in curl \u003c7.87.0. Curl can be asked to *tunnel* virtually all protocols it supports through an HTTP proxy. HTTP proxies can (and often do) deny such tunnel operations. When getting denied to tunnel the specific protocols SMB or TELNET, curl would use a heap-allocated struct after it had been freed, in its transfer shutdown code path."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2022-43552",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-43552\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libcurl4\nVersion: 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u3\nFix Version: 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u5\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2022-43552](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2022-43552)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2022-43552**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libcurl4  | 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u3  | 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u5  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2022-43552](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2022-43552)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl4@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u3?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-24540-go",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-24540 critical vulnerability for go package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Not all valid JavaScript whitespace characters are considered to be whitespace. Templates containing whitespace characters outside of the character set \"\\t\\n\\f\\r\\u0020\\u2028\\u2029\" in JavaScript contexts that also contain actions may not be properly sanitized during execution."
