              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42010-libgnutls30",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42010 critical vulnerability for libgnutls30 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in gnutls. Servers configured with RSA-PSK (Rivest–Shamir–Adleman – Pre-Shared Key) wrongfully matched usernames containing a NUL character with truncated usernames. A remote attacker could exploit this by sending a specially crafted username, leading to an authentication bypass. This vulnerability allows an attacker to gain unauthorized access by circumventing the authentication process."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42010",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42010\nSeverity: critical\nPackage: libgnutls30\nVersion: 3.7.1-5+deb11u2\nFix Version: 3.7.1-5+deb11u10\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-42010](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42010)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42010**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| critical  | libgnutls30  | 3.7.1-5+deb11u2  | 3.7.1-5+deb11u10  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-42010](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-42010)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libgnutls30@3.7.1-5%2Bdeb11u2?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=gnutls28"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-28321-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-28321 medium vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An improper certificate validation vulnerability exists in curl \u003cv8.1.0 in the way it supports matching of wildcard patterns when listed as \"Subject Alternative Name\" in TLS server certificates. curl can be built to use its own name matching function for TLS rather than one provided by a TLS library. This private wildcard matching function would match IDN (International Domain Name) hosts incorrectly and could as a result accept patterns that otherwise should mismatch. IDN hostnames are converted to puny code before used for certificate checks. Puny coded names always start with `xn--` and should not be allowed to pattern match, but the wildcard check in curl could still check for `x*`, which would match even though the IDN name most likely contained nothing even resembling an `x`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-28321",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-28321\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u3\nFix Version: 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u9\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2023-28321](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-28321)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-28321**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | curl  | 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u3  | 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u9  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2023-28321](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-28321)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u3?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-28321-libcurl3-gnutls",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-28321 medium vulnerability for libcurl3-gnutls package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An improper certificate validation vulnerability exists in curl \u003cv8.1.0 in the way it supports matching of wildcard patterns when listed as \"Subject Alternative Name\" in TLS server certificates. curl can be built to use its own name matching function for TLS rather than one provided by a TLS library. This private wildcard matching function would match IDN (International Domain Name) hosts incorrectly and could as a result accept patterns that otherwise should mismatch. IDN hostnames are converted to puny code before used for certificate checks. Puny coded names always start with `xn--` and should not be allowed to pattern match, but the wildcard check in curl could still check for `x*`, which would match even though the IDN name most likely contained nothing even resembling an `x`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-28321",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-28321\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libcurl3-gnutls\nVersion: 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u3\nFix Version: 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u9\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2023-28321](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-28321)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-28321**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libcurl3-gnutls  | 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u3  | 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u9  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2023-28321](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-28321)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libcurl3-gnutls@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u3?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=curl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9"
              }
            },
