            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-33846-libgnutls30",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-33846 high vulnerability for libgnutls30 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A heap buffer overflow vulnerability exists in the DTLS handshake fragment reassembly logic of GnuTLS. The issue arises in merge_handshake_packet() where incoming handshake fragments are matched and merged based solely on handshake type, without validating that the message_length field remains consistent across all fragments of the same logical message. An attacker can exploit this by sending crafted DTLS fragments with conflicting message_length values, causing the implementation to allocate a buffer based on a smaller initial fragment and subsequently write beyond its bounds using larger, inconsistent fragments. Because the merge operation does not enforce proper bounds checking against the allocated buffer size, this results in an out-of-bounds write on the heap. The vulnerability is remotely exploitable without authentication via the DTLS handshake path and can lead to application crashes or potential memory corruption."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-33846",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-33846\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libgnutls30\nVersion: 3.7.1-5+deb11u2\nFix Version: 3.7.1-5+deb11u10\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-33846](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-33846)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-33846**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libgnutls30  | 3.7.1-5+deb11u2  | 3.7.1-5+deb11u10  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-33846](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-33846)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libgnutls30@3.7.1-5%2Bdeb11u2?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=gnutls28"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45287-go",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-45287 high vulnerability for go package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Before Go 1.20, the RSA based TLS key exchanges used the math/big library, which is not constant time. RSA blinding was applied to prevent timing attacks, but analysis shows this may not have been fully effective. In particular it appears as if the removal of PKCS#1 padding may leak timing information, which in turn could be used to recover session key bits. In Go 1.20, the crypto/tls library switched to a fully constant time RSA implementation, which we do not believe exhibits any timing side channels."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45287",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-45287\nSeverity: high\nPackage: go\nVersion: 1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.20.0\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/go/bin/go\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2023-45287](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45287)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-45287**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | go  | 1.18.10  | 1.20.0  | binary  | /usr/local/go/bin/go  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2023-45287](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2023-45287)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/go@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-45287-stdlib",
              "name": "GoModuleMatcherExactDirectMatch",
