            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-23946-git",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-23946 high vulnerability for git package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Git, a revision control system, is vulnerable to path traversal prior to versions 2.39.2, 2.38.4, 2.37.6, 2.36.5, 2.35.7, 2.34.7, 2.33.7, 2.32.6, 2.31.7, and 2.30.8. By feeding a crafted input to `git apply`, a path outside the working tree can be overwritten as the user who is running `git apply`. A fix has been prepared and will appear in v2.39.2, v2.38.4, v2.37.6, v2.36.5, v2.35.7, v2.34.7, v2.33.7, v2.32.6, v2.31.7, and v2.30.8. As a workaround, use `git apply --stat` to inspect a patch before applying; avoid applying one that creates a symbolic link and then creates a file beyond the symbolic link."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-23946",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-23946\nSeverity: high\nPackage: git\nVersion: 1:2.30.2-1\nFix Version: 1:2.30.2-1+deb11u2\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2023-23946](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-23946)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-23946**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | git  | 1:2.30.2-1  | 1:2.30.2-1+deb11u2  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2023-23946](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2023-23946)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/git@1%3A2.30.2-1?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
