            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78659-go",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-78659 high vulnerability for go package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When \"Trailer\" headers are sent by a client, the HTTP server internally uses the header values to populate the Request.Trailer map passed to the server handler. Because Request.Trailer is a map, each entry incurs memory overhead. For HTTP/2 servers, a malicious client can exploit this by sending a \"Trailer\" header that declares a large number of fields, causing the server to allocate a disproportionate amount of memory while bypassing Server.MaxHeaderValueCount and Server.MaxHeaderBytes limits. This exploit is not applicable for HTTP/1 servers, which do not support multiplexing a large number of requests over one TCP connection, and whose Server.MaxHeaderBytes are calculated differently."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-78659",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-78659\nSeverity: high\nPackage: go\nVersion: 1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.26.9,1.27.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/go/bin/go\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-78659](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-78659)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-78659**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | go  | 1.18.10  | 1.26.9,1.27.2  | binary  | /usr/local/go/bin/go  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2026-78659](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-78659)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/go@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
