            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-0397-libpython3.9-stdlib",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-0397 high vulnerability for libpython3.9-stdlib package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A defect was discovered in the Python “ssl” module where there is a memory race condition with the ssl.SSLContext methods “cert_store_stats()” and “get_ca_certs()”. The race condition can be triggered if the methods are called at the same time as certificates are loaded into the SSLContext, such as during the TLS handshake with a certificate directory configured. This issue is fixed in CPython 3.10.14, 3.11.9, 3.12.3, and 3.13.0a5."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-0397",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-0397\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libpython3.9-stdlib\nVersion: 3.9.2-1\nFix Version: 3.9.2-1+deb11u2\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2024-0397](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-0397)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-0397**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libpython3.9-stdlib  | 3.9.2-1  | 3.9.2-1+deb11u2  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2024-0397](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-0397)  |\n"
