            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-61731-go",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-61731 high vulnerability for go package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Building a malicious file with cmd/go can cause can cause a write to an attacker-controlled file with partial control of the file content. The \"#cgo pkg-config:\" directive in a Go source file provides command-line arguments to provide to the Go pkg-config command. An attacker can provide a \"--log-file\" argument to this directive, causing pkg-config to write to an attacker-controlled location."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-61731",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-61731\nSeverity: high\nPackage: go\nVersion: 1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.24.12,1.25.6\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/go/bin/go\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-61731](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-61731)",
