            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78660-go",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-78660 high vulnerability for go package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Historically, we have been rather lax about malformed framing-related headers in our HTTP/2 implementation, as they cannot interfere with HTTP/2 framing. However, this makes it possible for our HTTP/2 implementation to forward responses containing such headers to an HTTP/1 client when acting as a reverse proxy. If the HTTP/1 client also does not behave strictly enough, this can result in response smuggling."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-78660",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-78660\nSeverity: high\nPackage: go\nVersion: 1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.26.9,1.27.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/go/bin/go\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-78660](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-78660)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-78660**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | go  | 1.18.10  | 1.26.9,1.27.2  | binary  | /usr/local/go/bin/go  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2026-78660](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-78660)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/go@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78660-stdlib",
