            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-6253-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-6253 medium vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "curl might erroneously pass on credentials for a first proxy to a second proxy.  This can happen when the following conditions are true:  1. curl is setup to use specific different proxies for different URL schemes 2. the first proxy needs credentials 3. the second proxy uses no credentials 4. while using the first proxy (using say `http://`), curl is asked to follow    a redirect to a URL using another scheme (say `https://`), accessed using a    second, different, proxy"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-6253",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-6253\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-6253](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-6253)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-6253**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | curl  | 7.74.0-1.3+deb11u3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-6253](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-6253)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@7.74.0-1.3%2Bdeb11u3?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9"
              }
            },
