            {
              "id": "CVE-2024-28834-libgnutls30",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2024-28834 medium vulnerability for libgnutls30 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GnuTLS. The Minerva attack is a cryptographic vulnerability that exploits deterministic behavior in systems like GnuTLS, leading to side-channel leaks. In specific scenarios, such as when using the GNUTLS_PRIVKEY_FLAG_REPRODUCIBLE flag, it can result in a noticeable step in nonce size from 513 to 512 bits, exposing a potential timing side-channel."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-28834",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2024-28834\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libgnutls30\nVersion: 3.7.1-5+deb11u2\nFix Version: 3.7.1-5+deb11u6\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2024-28834](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-28834)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2024-28834**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libgnutls30  | 3.7.1-5+deb11u2  | 3.7.1-5+deb11u6  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2024-28834](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2024-28834)  |\n"
              },
