            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-15661-libssh2-1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-15661 medium vulnerability for libssh2-1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libssh2 through 1.11.1, fixed in commit 2dae302, contains an out-of-bounds heap read vulnerability in the sftp_symlink() function in src/sftp.c that allows a malicious SSH server or man-in-the-middle attacker to disclose heap memory contents or cause a crash by sending a crafted SSH_FXP_NAME response. Attackers can supply a link_len value larger than the actual packet data in SSH_FXP_NAME responses for SFTP READLINK and REALPATH operations, triggering a heap buffer over-read of up to target_len minus one bytes due to the missing validation of available packet buffer size before the memcpy operation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-15661",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-15661\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libssh2-1\nVersion: 1.9.0-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2025-15661](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-15661)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-15661**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libssh2-1  | 1.9.0-2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2025-15661](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-15661)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libssh2-1@1.9.0-2?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=libssh2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-37454-libpython3.9-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-37454 low vulnerability for libpython3.9-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The Keccak XKCP SHA-3 reference implementation before fdc6fef has an integer overflow and resultant buffer overflow that allows attackers to execute arbitrary code or eliminate expected cryptographic properties. This occurs in the sponge function interface."
