            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-66034-libssh2-1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-66034 high vulnerability for libssh2-1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libssh2 through 1.11.1, fixed in commit a13bb6c, contains a missing bounds check vulnerability that allows a malicious SSH server to trigger an arbitrary-length heap out-of-bounds read and a free of an uninitialized pointer via the publickey subsystem. In libssh2_publickey_list_fetch(), the version 1 response parser reads a server-controlled comment_len value and advances the parse pointer without verifying sufficient bytes remain in the buffer, causing the out-of-bounds read to leak heap pointers from adjacent allocations defeating ASLR, followed by heap allocator state corruption when the error cleanup path frees an uninitialized pointer from a non-zeroed realloc() region."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66034",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-66034\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libssh2-1\nVersion: 1.9.0-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-66034](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66034)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-66034**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libssh2-1  | 1.9.0-2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-66034](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-66034)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libssh2-1@1.9.0-2?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=libssh2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-1299-libpython3.9-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-1299 medium vulnerability for libpython3.9-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The  email module, specifically the \"BytesGenerator\" class, didn’t properly quote newlines for email headers when  serializing an email message allowing for header injection when an email  is serialized. This is only applicable if using \"LiteralHeader\" writing headers that don't respect email folding rules, the new behavior will reject the incorrectly folded headers in \"BytesGenerator\"."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-1299",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-1299\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpython3.9-minimal\nVersion: 3.9.2-1\nFix Version: 3.9.2-1+deb11u5\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-1299](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-1299)",
