              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/wget@1.21-1%2Bdeb11u1?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-58471-wget",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-58471 high vulnerability for wget package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU Wget through 1.25.0, fixed in commit c2640fe, contains a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the convert_fname() function within src/url.c that allows remote attackers to trigger memory corruption through a server-supplied filename requiring character set conversion. When the output buffer is too small during iconv E2BIG reallocation, the reallocation logic miscalculates the remaining space, leading to a heap buffer overflow that can be exploited via a maliciously crafted server response."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-58471",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-58471\nSeverity: high\nPackage: wget\nVersion: 1.21-1+deb11u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-58471](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-58471)",
