            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-13601-libglib2.0-0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-13601 high vulnerability for libglib2.0-0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A heap-based buffer overflow problem was found in glib through an incorrect calculation of buffer size in the g_escape_uri_string() function. If the string to escape contains a very large number of unacceptable characters (which would need escaping), the calculation of the length of the escaped string could overflow, leading to a potential write off the end of the newly allocated string."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-13601",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-13601\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libglib2.0-0\nVersion: 2.66.8-1\nFix Version: 2.66.8-1+deb11u7\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2025-13601](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-13601)",
