              "id": "CVE-2026-35386-openssh-client",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-35386 high vulnerability for openssh-client package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "In OpenSSH before 10.3, command execution can occur via shell metacharacters in a username within a command line. This requires a scenario where the username on the command line is untrusted, and also requires a non-default configurations of % in ssh_config."
