            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-8328-libpython3.9-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-8328 medium vulnerability for libpython3.9-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The ftpcp() function in Lib/ftplib.py was not updated when  CVE-2021-4189 was fixed. While makepasv() was patched to replace  server-supplied PASV host addresses with the actual peer address  (getpeername()[0]), ftpcp() still calls parse227() directly and passes  the raw attacker-controllable IP address and port to target.sendport(). This patch is related to CVE-2021-4189."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8328",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-8328\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpython3.9-minimal\nVersion: 3.9.2-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-8328](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-8328)",
