            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-58051-libssh2-1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-58051 high vulnerability for libssh2-1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libssh2 through 1.11.1 grows its publickey list with SSH2_REALLOC but does not zero-initialize new entries before parsing populates them, so a parse failure reaching the cleanup path leaves libssh2_publickey_list_free operating on an uninitialized entry. A malicious SSH server offering the publickey subsystem can use a malformed response to make cleanup free an uninitialized, attacker-influenceable attrs pointer in a connecting libssh2 client."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-58051",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-58051\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libssh2-1\nVersion: 1.9.0-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-58051](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-58051)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-58051**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libssh2-1  | 1.9.0-2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-58051](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-58051)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libssh2-1@1.9.0-2?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=libssh2"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-19499-libc-bin",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-19499 high vulnerability for libc-bin package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Calling strfmon and strfmon_l in the GNU C Library version 2.38 to 2.44 can write past the end of the caller-supplied output buffer when a conversion uses right-justified width padding.\n\nExploitation requires an application code path that calls strfmon or strfmon_l with right-justified width padding into a destination buffer that is large enough for the padding to succeed but too small for the internal memmove call. The field width or format may be attacker-influenced or a fixed susceptible pattern in the caller.\n\nAt the time of publication, no network-facing application impact is known."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-19499",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-19499\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libc-bin\nVersion: 2.31-13+deb11u5\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-19499](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-19499)",
