            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-57432-libperl5.32",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-57432 high vulnerability for libperl5.32 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions through 5.43.10 have an integer overflow in S_measure_struct leading to an out-of-bounds heap read in pack and unpack.  S_measure_struct adds each item's size times its repeat count to a running total with no overflow check, so a large repeat count in a pack or unpack template wraps the signed SSize_t total negative. The @, X, and x position codes then guard their moves with a signed length comparison that passes when the length is negative, advancing the buffer pointer out of bounds.  A template derived from untrusted input can read heap memory past the buffer and return it to the caller."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-57432",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-57432\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libperl5.32\nVersion: 5.32.1-4+deb11u2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-57432](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-57432)",
