            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-1795-python3.9-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-1795 low vulnerability for python3.9-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "During an address list folding when a separating comma ends up on a folded line and that line is to be unicode-encoded then the separator itself is also unicode-encoded. Expected behavior is that the separating comma remains a plan comma. This can result in the address header being misinterpreted by some mail servers."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-1795",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-1795\nSeverity: low\nPackage: python3.9-minimal\nVersion: 3.9.2-1\nFix Version: 3.9.2-1+deb11u3\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2025-1795](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-1795)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-1795**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | python3.9-minimal  | 3.9.2-1  | 3.9.2-1+deb11u3  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2025-1795](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-1795)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/python3.9-minimal@3.9.2-1?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=python3.9"
                ],
                "security-severity": "2.3"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-32289-go",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-32289 medium vulnerability for go package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Context was not properly tracked across template branches for JS template literals, leading to possibly incorrect escaping of content when branches were used. Additionally template actions within JS template literals did not properly track the brace depth, leading to incorrect escaping being applied. These issues could cause actions within JS template literals to be incorrectly or improperly escaped, leading to XSS vulnerabilities."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-32289",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-32289\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: go\nVersion: 1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.25.9,1.26.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/go/bin/go\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-32289](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-32289)",
