                "text": "The client side in OpenSSH 5.7 through 8.4 has an Observable Discrepancy leading to an information leak in the algorithm negotiation. This allows man-in-the-middle attackers to target initial connection attempts (where no host key for the server has been cached by the client). NOTE: some reports state that 8.5 and 8.6 are also affected."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2020-14145",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2020-14145\nSeverity: low\nPackage: openssh-client\nVersion: 1:8.4p1-5+deb11u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2020-14145](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2020-14145)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2020-14145**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | openssh-client  | 1:8.4p1-5+deb11u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2020-14145](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2020-14145)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/openssh-client@1%3A8.4p1-5%2Bdeb11u1?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=openssh"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.9"
              }
