            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53615-bsdutils",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-53615 high vulnerability for bsdutils package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux is a random collection of Linux utilities. Before util-linux 2.41.4, `parse_dos_extended()` in `libblkid/src/partitions/dos.c` computes an extended-partition start sector with 32-bit addition and does not apply the extended-area bounds checks to the first two EBR entries. A local attacker who causes a crafted DOS extended-partition disk image or removable medium to be probed can wrap `cur_start + start` to sector zero and cause libblkid to report a false partition overlapping the MBR. This directly compromises the integrity of the reported partition metadata; disk modification or availability loss requires a separate downstream consumer to act on that metadata. This issue is fixed in 2.41.4."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53615",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53615\nSeverity: high\nPackage: bsdutils\nVersion: 1:2.36.1-8+deb11u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-53615](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53615)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53615**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | bsdutils  | 1:2.36.1-8+deb11u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-53615](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53615)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/bsdutils@1%3A2.36.1-8%2Bdeb11u1?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=util-linux%402.36.1-8%2Bdeb11u1"
