            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53613-bsdutils",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-53613 high vulnerability for bsdutils package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux is a random collection of Linux utilities. In util-linux 2.17 through 2.41.6 and 2.42 through 2.42.3, and in 2.42.4 when the legacy `mount(2)` path is used without `/proc`, restricted non-root `mount` requests validate an `/etc/fstab` target before the mount operation re-resolves that pathname. A local low-privileged user authorized by an fstab `user` or `users` entry whose target has an attacker-writable ancestor can use `renameat2(RENAME_EXCHANGE)` to swap a path component and redirect an authorized mount to a root-owned location, such as mounting attacker-controlled content over `/etc/sudoers.d`, and thereby gain root privileges. Versions 2.41.5 and 2.42.2 pin targets for the new mount API, and 2.42.4 pins legacy targets through `/proc/self/fd`; the documented legacy fallback without `/proc` remains affected."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53613",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53613\nSeverity: high\nPackage: bsdutils\nVersion: 1:2.36.1-8+deb11u1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-53613](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53613)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53613**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | bsdutils  | 1:2.36.1-8+deb11u1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-53613](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53613)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/bsdutils@1%3A2.36.1-8%2Bdeb11u1?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=util-linux%402.36.1-8%2Bdeb11u1"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53613-libblkid1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-53613 high vulnerability for libblkid1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux is a random collection of Linux utilities. In util-linux 2.17 through 2.41.6 and 2.42 through 2.42.3, and in 2.42.4 when the legacy `mount(2)` path is used without `/proc`, restricted non-root `mount` requests validate an `/etc/fstab` target before the mount operation re-resolves that pathname. A local low-privileged user authorized by an fstab `user` or `users` entry whose target has an attacker-writable ancestor can use `renameat2(RENAME_EXCHANGE)` to swap a path component and redirect an authorized mount to a root-owned location, such as mounting attacker-controlled content over `/etc/sudoers.d`, and thereby gain root privileges. Versions 2.41.5 and 2.42.2 pin targets for the new mount API, and 2.42.4 pins legacy targets through `/proc/self/fd`; the documented legacy fallback without `/proc` remains affected."
              },
