            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-54369-libacl1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-54369 high vulnerability for libacl1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "acl before version 2.4.0 contains a symlink traversal vulnerability in the libacl pathname-based functions acl_get_file(), acl_set_file(), acl_extended_file(), and acl_delete_def_file() that allows local attackers to escalate privileges by replacing any pathname component with a symbolic link. Attackers who control any component of a pathname processed by a privileged caller can redirect ACL read or write operations to arbitrary files or directories, enabling unauthorized manipulation of access control lists and local privilege escalation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-54369",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-54369\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libacl1\nVersion: 2.2.53-10\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-54369](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-54369)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-54369**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libacl1  | 2.2.53-10  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-54369](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-54369)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libacl1@2.2.53-10?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=acl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-4519-libpython3.9-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-4519 low vulnerability for libpython3.9-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The webbrowser.open() API would accept leading dashes in the URL which  could be handled as command line options for certain web browsers. New  behavior rejects leading dashes. Users are recommended to sanitize URLs  prior to passing to webbrowser.open()."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-4519",
