            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-94444-go",
              "name": "StockMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-94444 high vulnerability for go package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Previously, a user operating inside of a malicious Go project that defines a bogus golang.org/fips140 and operates a malicious GOMODPROXY the user chooses to connect to can serve an arbitrary module in its place. We now unpack the trusted ziphash for the bundled golang.org/fips140 module and construct its entry in the GOMODCACHE such that it can be verified by the toolchain."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-94444",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-94444\nSeverity: high\nPackage: go\nVersion: 1.18.10\nFix Version: 1.26.9,1.27.2\nType: binary\nLocation: /usr/local/go/bin/go\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2026-94444](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-94444)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-94444**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | go  | 1.18.10  | 1.26.9,1.27.2  | binary  | /usr/local/go/bin/go  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2026-94444](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-94444)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:generic/go@1.18.10"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.8"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2020-13529-libsystemd0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2020-13529 low vulnerability for libsystemd0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An exploitable denial-of-service vulnerability exists in Systemd 245. A specially crafted DHCP FORCERENEW packet can cause a server running the DHCP client to be vulnerable to a DHCP ACK spoofing attack. An attacker can forge a pair of FORCERENEW and DCHP ACK packets to reconfigure the server."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2020-13529",
