                "text": "CVE-2026-29111 medium vulnerability for libudev1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "systemd, a system and service manager, (as PID 1) hits an assert and freezes execution when an unprivileged IPC API call is made with spurious data. On version v249 and older the effect is not an assert, but stack overwriting, with the attacker controlled content. From version v250 and newer this is not possible as the safety check causes an assert instead. This IPC call was added in v239, so versions older than that are not affected. Versions 260-rc1, 259.2, 258.5, and 257.11 contain patches. No known workarounds are available."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-29111",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-29111\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libudev1\nVersion: 247.3-7+deb11u1\nFix Version: 247.3-7+deb11u8\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-29111](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-29111)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-29111**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libudev1  | 247.3-7+deb11u1  | 247.3-7+deb11u8  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-29111](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-29111)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libudev1@247.3-7%2Bdeb11u1?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=systemd"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-15649-libperl5.32",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-15649 medium vulnerability for libperl5.32 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "IO::Uncompress::Unzip versions before 2.215 for Perl propagate uncaught exception when parsing zip header with malformed DOS date.  _dosToUnixTime() decodes the local-file-header last-modification date field and calls Time::Local::timelocal() without an eval guard. A header whose date field decodes to an out-of-range month, day, or hour causes timelocal() to die.  The exception propagates out of IO::Uncompress::Unzip-\u003enew($file) where callers expect undef plus $UnzipError."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-15649",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-15649\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libperl5.32\nVersion: 5.32.1-4+deb11u2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2025-15649](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-15649)",
