            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-11940-libpython3.9-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-11940 low vulnerability for libpython3.9-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "tarfile.extractall() with the 'data' or 'tar'  filter could be bypassed by a crafted archive where a hardlink  references a symlink stored at a deeper name than the hardlink itself.   The extraction fallback validated the symlink at it's archived location  but recreated it at the hardlink's shallower path, letting a relative  target the filter judged contained escape the destination directory.   This allowed a malicious tar archive to create a symlink pointing  outside the destination, enabling out-of-destination file reads or  writes. This was an incomplete fix of CVE-2025-4330."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11940",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-11940\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libpython3.9-minimal\nVersion: 3.9.2-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-11940](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11940)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-11940**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libpython3.9-minimal  | 3.9.2-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-11940](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-11940)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libpython3.9-minimal@3.9.2-1?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6\u0026upstream=python3.9"
