            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-5958-sed",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-5958 low vulnerability for sed package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When sed is invoked with both -i (in-place edit) and --follow-symlinks, the function open_next_file() performs two separate, non-atomic filesystem operations on the same path:  1. resolves symlink to its target and stores the resolved path for determining when output is written, 2. opens the original symlink path (not the resolved one) to read the file.  Between these two calls there is a race window. If an attacker atomically replaces the symlink with a different target during that window, sed will: read content from the new (attacker-chosen) symlink target and write the processed result to the path recorded in step 1. This can lead to arbitrary file overwrite with attacker-controlled content in the context of the sed process.   This issue was fixed in version 4.10."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-5958",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-5958\nSeverity: low\nPackage: sed\nVersion: 4.7-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-5958](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-5958)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-5958**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | sed  | 4.7-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-5958](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-5958)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/sed@4.7-1?arch=arm64\u0026distro=debian-11.6"
                ],
                "security-severity": "2.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-1181-binutils",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-1181 low vulnerability for binutils package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability classified as critical was found in GNU Binutils 2.43. This vulnerability affects the function _bfd_elf_gc_mark_rsec of the file bfd/elflink.c of the component ld. The manipulation leads to memory corruption. The attack can be initiated remotely. The complexity of an attack is rather high. The exploitation appears to be difficult. The exploit has been disclosed to the public and may be used. The name of the patch is 931494c9a89558acb36a03a340c01726545eef24. It is recommended to apply a patch to fix this issue."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-1181",
