            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-4516-libpython3.9-minimal",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-4516 low vulnerability for libpython3.9-minimal package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "There is an issue in CPython when using `bytes.decode(\"unicode_escape\", error=\"ignore|replace\")`. If you are not using the \"unicode_escape\" encoding or an error handler your usage is not affected. To work-around this issue you may stop using the error= handler and instead wrap the bytes.decode() call in a try-except catching the DecodeError."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-4516",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-4516\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libpython3.9-minimal\nVersion: 3.9.2-1\nFix Version: 3.9.2-1+deb11u4\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2025-4516](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2025-4516)",
