            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-15003-binutils-common",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-15003 low vulnerability for binutils-common package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in the GNU Binutils (Binary Utilities) linker. This vulnerability, a heap-buffer-overflow read (CWE-125), occurs when the linker processes a specially crafted 32-bit XCOFF (Extended Common Object File Format) object file. An attacker could exploit this by providing a malicious file, leading to an out-of-bounds read of memory. This can result in information disclosure, potentially revealing sensitive heap data, and a Denial of Service (DoS) due to the linker crashing."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15003",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-15003\nSeverity: low\nPackage: binutils-common\nVersion: 2.35.2-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:11\nLink: [CVE-2026-15003](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15003)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-15003**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | binutils-common  | 2.35.2-2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:11  | [CVE-2026-15003](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15003)  |\n"
              },
